## Donut Chart

**Donut Chart**: a self-contained SVG donut with no chart library. `@segments` ({label, value, color}[]) plus optional `@centerValue`, `@centerLabel`, `@formatValue` and `@onSelect`. Renders proportional stroke arcs, a center figure, and a swatch legend with per-segment counts and percentages.

```gts
import { DonutChart, type DonutSegment } from '@cardstack/catalog/components/donut-chart';

<DonutChart
  @segments={{this.statusSegments}}
  @centerValue='67%'
  @centerLabel='of released work'
  @onSelect={{this.filterByStatus}}
/>
```

**The block does not know what a status or a category is.** Segments arrive labeled and colored by the consumer; zero-value segments are dropped from arcs and legend so an empty category never renders a 0% sliver. Learner Progress feeds it a learner's work by status; any consumer with a part-of-whole breakdown can feed it something else.

With `@onSelect`, each legend row is a button that calls it with the segment's label, so the consumer can filter by it. A segment colour that is not a plain CSS colour falls back to the text colour.

Arcs are plain `stroke-dasharray` circles — no path math, no animation dependency — so the component renders identically in prerender and live contexts.

**Non-goals:** hover tooltips, the filtering UI itself (the consumer owns it), multiple rings, and percentage-label placement inside arcs at small sizes.
